{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And what remains in the blood shall be drained.</b> He circles the place of pinching toward the altar and presses it against the wall, and the blood drains out and runs down to the foundation. It is written with an alef, which also implies regarding the sprinkling, that automatically blood shall be present at the wall; so it is taught, and so the commentator explained in Zevaḥim, in the chapter Kodshei Kodashim."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:10:06.534096842Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}